From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hmos2sweet <hmos2sweet@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] icnss: send the cal report after a rejected BDF completion

The WCN3990 firmware answers the last BDF segment (the one with end=1) with
result=1 error=1 even when it accepted the image. On sagit that was proven by
capturing the vendor cnss-daemon's own accepted transactions over the legacy
ipc-router: its four requests are byte-for-byte what we send, its completion
is rejected the same way, and what releases the firmware is the CAL_REPORT it
sends next -- READY_IND follows about 100 ms later. wlfw_send_bdf() treated any
non-success as fatal and returned before icnss_sweet_download_bdf() reached the
cal report, so the download was logged as failed and FW_READY never arrived.

Only a rejection on a segment that is not the last one is a real failure.
---
diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/icnss_qmi.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/icnss_qmi.c
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/icnss_qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/icnss_qmi.c
@@ -488,10 +488,16 @@
 		ret = qmi_txn_wait(&txn, WLFW_TIMEOUT);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			goto out;
 		if (resp->resp.result != QMI_RESULT_SUCCESS_V01) {
-			icnss_pr_err("sweet: BDF segment %u rejected, result %d error %d\n",
-				     seg - 1, resp->resp.result, resp->resp.error);
-			ret = -EINVAL;
-			goto out;
+			/* The completion segment (end = 1) is answered with
+			 * result=1 error=1 by WCN3990 even when the image was
+			 * accepted -- the vendor cnss-daemon gets the same reply.
+			 * The firmware leaves its download state on the
+			 * calibration report, so this is only a failure before
+			 * the last segment. */
+			icnss_pr_err("sweet: BDF segment %u answered result %d error %d\n",
+				     seg - 1, resp->resp.result, resp->resp.error);
+			ret = req->end ? 0 : -EINVAL;
+			goto out;
 		}
 		left -= n;
-- 
